SUMMARY:The Invincible - Stanisław Lem
DESCRIPTION:The Sci Fi Book Club\nHi everybody\,\n\nSeptember's pick was j
 ust as popular as *Blindsight* on our survey. Our outer-space mystery seri
 es continues with our highest-voted classic in a while\, Stanisław Lem's 
 eponymous *The Invincible* is supposed to be a wild ride.\n\nAs a reminder
 \, we skip our October book each year to highlight the [Brooklyn SciFi Fil
 m Festival](https://brooklynscififilmfest.com/). The BSFFF is back for its
  7th installment\, with films streaming online and screening in person thr
 oughout the week. I'll share more information about the different events a
 nd ways to participate in September. I hope you'll join us!\n\nBook of the
  Month\n*The Invincible* \\- Stanisław Lem \\(1964\\)\n\n*The Invincible*
  is considered one of Stanisław Lem's defining novels and another true cl
 assic of science fiction. We're back aboard a starship this month\, follow
 ing a crew sent to investigate the disappearance of an expedition on a dis
 tant planet. It's a mystery wrapped in world-building\, atmospheric explor
 ation\, and the kind of ideas that made Lem such an influential voice in t
 he genre.\n\nBook Club has really enjoyed the Lem stories we've read so fa
 r\, can't wait to dive into one of the novels that put him on the map. Urs
 ula K. Le Guin said about *The Invincible*: "Anybody who likes a mystery w
 ill find it here — and its solution."\n\nTo join a Book Club meeting\, a
 ll you will need is YOURSELF. If you haven’t had a chance to finish the 
 book\, we still would love for you to join us in the discussion.\n\nNot ab
 le to join us in person for events? [The Sci Fi Book Club is on Discord](h
 ttps://discord.gg/B9NMnC2F). Join us and keep the conversation going.
